WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.813
Two infrastructure pieces
join the foundation.

2
00:00:02.813 --> 00:00:04.637
First, address management.

3
00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:07.627
Many agencies track IP
ranges in a spreadsheet,

4
00:00:07.627 --> 00:00:11.076
and that's where conflicts
and ghost records come from.

5
00:00:11.076 --> 00:00:16.291
Phase one puts the platform host and
the most critical infrastructure under

6
00:00:16.291 --> 00:00:21.100
one governed address authority, so
DNS and DHCP can later derive from it.

7
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.662
Second, servers.

8
00:00:22.662 --> 00:00:25.040
Intune doesn't manage Windows Server,

9
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.488
so the platform host and a few pilot
servers connect through Azure Arc.

10
00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:32.459
Each gets a cloud identity,
a security baseline,

11
00:00:32.459 --> 00:00:36.720
patching and protection, without
changing its domain membership.
